## Scope your comment to the right discussion

Sub-entities ({{ _hosted_plurals | join(', ') }})
each have their own discussion region alongside the parent item's main discussion. Use
`sq <type> <n> <kind> <k> comment` for anything scoped to that one sub-entity; use
`sq <type> <n> comment` for cross-cutting material that applies to the whole item.

| Scope | Command | When to use |
|---|---|---|
{% for _kind in _kind_to_type %}
| One {{ _kind }} | `sq {{ _kind_to_type[_kind] }} <n> {{ _kind }} <k> comment` | Notes scoped to this {{ _kind }}: a clarification, blocker or question local to it |
{% endfor %}
| Whole item | `sq <type> <n> comment` | Handoff @mentions, decisions spanning multiple sub-entities, item-level status summaries |

@mentions are surfaced by `sq inbox` wherever they live in the file — in a sub-entity discussion
or the main one. Prefer the main discussion for @mentions that announce a transition or request
action from the next agent (they read as item-level handoffs); a sub-entity discussion is fine for
a scoped question (e.g. `sq {{ anchor or "<type>" }} N {{ anchor_kind or "<kind>" }} 1 comment
--as <your-slug> -m "@role does this look right?"`). This is guidance, not a hard rule — the
inbox never misses a mention.

## Common commands

```bash
sq create {{ anchor or "<type>" }} "Title" --author <your-slug>{% if anchor_parent_prefix %} [--parent {{ anchor_parent_prefix }}-<n>]{% endif %} [-m "body…"]  # also: {{ spec.non_roster_types() | reject('eq', anchor) | sort | join('|') }}
#   --author is required and must be a registered agent (your own role slug)
sq {{ anchor or "<type>" }} 3 show --full --comments                                # full dossier: body + sub-entities + discussion
sq {{ anchor or "<type>" }} 3 status {{ anchor_active or anchor_settled or "<status>" }}                                     # transition (validated per type)
sq {{ anchor or "<type>" }} 3 update --assignee {{ example_assignee_slug(source.roster, source.developer_slugs) }}{% if _priority_field %} --{{ _priority_field.code }} {{ _priority_values[0] }}{% endif %}{% if anchor_parent_prefix %} --parent {{ anchor_parent_prefix }}-<n>{% endif %}  # metadata (parent validated)
sq {{ anchor or "<type>" }} 3 body -m "## Description" -m "…"                        # set the body (or --file)
sq {{ anchor or "<type>" }} 3 comment --as <your-slug> -m "…"                        # discussion / @mentions (or --file)
sq {{ anchor or "<type>" }} 3 comment <hash> edit --as <your-slug> -m "…"           # correct your own comment (also show, remove)
sq list --type {{ anchor or "<type>" }} --status {{ anchor_active or anchor_settled or "<status>" }}                         # closed items hidden; --all to include
sq tree {{ anchor_parent_prefix or anchor_prefix }}-<n> --json                                      # a parent's whole subtree (status/blocked) for coordinating
sq search "lockout"                                             # match titles, summaries, bodies
sq mine <your-slug>                                             # your open items  ·  sq workload
sq blocked                                                      # open items waiting on an open blocker
sq docs [internals|workflow|migration|...]                      # read the full docs in-terminal (offline)
```

Items whose status is hidden-by-default (typically the settled/closed ones) drop out of `sq
list`/`sq tree` — pass `--all` or an explicit `--status` to see them.{% if _priority_field %} Set importance with `--{{ _priority_field.code }} {{ _priority_values | join('|') }}`.{% endif +%}

Run `sq --help`, `sq <type> --help`, or `sq <type> <n> --help` for the full surface.

